      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s early nickname was “Midway,” because it sat halfway between Lula and Harmony Grove, now Commerce, in 1847.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://theforgottensouth.com/skeleton-house-georgia-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1919 Maysville hosted a cottonseed oil plant, a fertilizer plant, and a chair factory, marking a brief industrial boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
